# Architecture Rules

When you are asked to build out any new functionality that spans multiple modules with lots of repeating logic (horizontal data) - focus on identifying the the repetitive patterns and getting just ONE of them right as a proof of concept before scaling.

It is much easier to scale an app when you get the core logic correct first. Let's call this a vertical-first approach. Always get the integration/business/package logic and module interactions in place before building out horizontally.
